    "deckDescription": "Eight 40-card stripped decks (320 cards total): each deck is a standard 52-card pack with 8s, 9s, and 10s removed. Used for Panguingue (Pan), where players meld sets and runs and the first to meld 11 cards goes out; conditions like valle cards and ace/king sets earn chip payouts.",
    "suitDescription": "The four French suits (hearts, diamonds, clubs, spades) appear in each of the eight 40-card decks; each suit has seven ranks (Ace, King, Queen, Jack, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2). Melds are sets of three or more of the same rank or runs in the same suit.",
    "rankDescription": "In each suit, ranks are Ace, King, Queen, Jack, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 (no 8, 9, 10). Multiple decks mean multiple copies of each card; melds use cards from any deck. Aces can count high or low in runs; valle (2s) and other conditions have special payout rules.",
